# Pinned from the real red run of 2026-07-29 with the injection applied.
#
# The injection removes the file-identity cache from `RunCatalog::refresh_dir`:
# every inventory pass and every daemon boot re-derives every record from disk,
# which is exactly what the pre-catalog code did on every call.
exit: 101

# THE COST CLAIM. After the one-time legacy index, enumerating a 197-file
# production-shaped board must read no session bytes at all. Without the cache
# it reads 2.4 MiB of bounded windows on the small board and 27 MiB on the 16x
# board — a cost that is still a function of what the files contain.
contains: enumeration after the index still read session bytes

# THE SAME CLAIM'S OTHER HALF. Every record of an unchanged board is answered
# from the catalog; a cache-hit count of zero is the pre-catalog behaviour.
contains: every record of an unchanged board must be answered from the catalog

# BOOT RECONCILIATION. The second boot must load the previous boot's durable
# index and re-read only what was written since. Without the cache the snapshot
# is loaded and then ignored, so the restart pays the whole board again.
contains: the first boot indexed the board

# All three, and only these three. A binary that collapses wholesale is a
# different failure and has not reproduced this defect.
contains: test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 3 failed
